# A pile of cards
A game's stock, its discards, a column on the table:  the game names its piles, and says what each kind takes.
Each pile is its own element around its cards' elements, `<solitaire-tableau>` around `<solitaire-card>`s.
A card dragged over it glows when it would take the card, by its own rules (`droppable`).

<view "pile" template="viewable list of cards" droppable>
	<property "name" description="What the game calls it, e.g. stock">text</>
	<property "layout" one-of="stacked, vertical, horizontal or fanned"
		description="How its cards lie:  on top of each other, down a column, along a row, or fanned as a hand is held -- styles.css"
	/>
	<property "color" description="Its last card's:  what the next card goes on">
		"none" if it is empty
		the color of its last card otherwise
	</>
	<property "value" description="Its last card's">
		0 if it is empty
		the value of its last card otherwise
	</>
	<property "state" description="Its name, then its cards' short names:  stock: Q♠↑ 7♥↓">
		set summary to (its name or "pile") + ":"
		for card in the pile
			set summary to summary + " " + the state of the card
		return summary
	</>

	<test "piles">
		set the stock to a new pile with name = "stock"
		the stock's color should be "none"
		the stock's value should be 0
		add (a new card whose rank is queen, suit is spades and direction is up) to the stock
		add (a new card whose rank is 7, suit is hearts and direction is down) to the stock
		the stock's color should be red
		the stock's value should be 7
		the stock's state should be "stock: Q♠↑ 7♥↓"

		// a card is in one pile at a time
		set the discards to a new pile with name = "discards"
		get the last card of the stock
		add it to the discards
		its pile is the discards should be yes
		the number of cards in the stock should be 1
		the discards' state should be "discards: 7♥↓"
	</>
</>

<spell>
	// a card is in one pile at a time:  putting it on another pile takes it off this one
	a card belongs to one pile
</>
